  "agent": {
    "note": "**v1 PROD GATE — `@m0saic/media/barcode/v1`** (gate 18 — media pack remainder opens; chart: `.ai/LAUNCH/v1-template-cut.md`). Props = showcase defaults (Code 128 \"M0SAIC\", light, HRI on).\n\n| Stage | Current | Proposed |\n|---|---|---|\n| Flags | not internal, not deprecated, NOT primitive | confirm |\n| Gate | — | **base** |\n| Preview assets | see history line above the table in chat | review |\n| Cover / Tutorial | NO cover built — the default render IS the final face (static image, no intro): first-open shows the barcode instantly | confirm none needed |\n\n**Pre-audit found + fixed 1 (the bg-drop again, at its worst):**\n- **Light mode rendered as a SCANNABILITY INVERSION through .mosaicx**: black canvas, orange bars, white HRI patches — the quiet-zone ground lives in doc.backgroundColor only, which template_invocation flattening drops (candidate 2026-08-06). Solid modes now ALSO paint the ground as a real base tile (prepended after the HRI splice so indices hold); transparent mode stays tile-free so alpha survives. Third confirmed template on this candidate (donut, line-chart, stat-card, now barcode).\n\n**Known constraints (documented, not fixed):**\n1. **Long payloads refuse at narrow canvases** (42-char Code 128 at 360/480px wide → sub-pixel bars → engine min-size culls everything → exit 1 \"no media sources\"). Data physics: a scannable barcode can't shrink below ~1px/module. Same ugly-failure class as the nested-error-black candidate. Battery is 82/84 with these two documented refusals.\n2. Through .mosaicx the barcode STRETCHES to the host canvas (flatten ignores the declared natural size) — bars stay proportionally correct (ratio splits) so scannability holds, but the aspect follows the canvas. Pre-existing, direct renders honor natural dims.\n3. fps/durationMs are nominal constants (image output) — left as-is to avoid shifting goldens for zero user value.\n\n**No layout contract added** (deliberate): geometry is generator-driven (dsl-stdlib barcodeToRenderable) and locked by the existing e2e + visual goldens; HRI fonts are band-height-derived and structurally safe (payload growth widens the canvas faster than the caption).\n\n**Primitive-sense: NOT primitive** — a media utility (the metadata-stamp class).\n\nBattery 82/84 ×2 (2 documented refusals), jest 19/19 (1 spec updated to lock the base tile).",
    "question": "Default look verdict? No-cover call OK? Long-payload narrow-canvas refusal acceptable as documented physics? NOT-primitive confirmed? Then stress.",
    "response": {
      "verdict": "ship",
      "text": "default pass + no-cover call accepted (\"good, lets stress\") -> stress x10 pass -> \"pass, ship it\"",
      "via": "chat — transcribed by agent",
      "note": "SHIPPED base ☑ (gate 18, media pack remainder 1/n). NOT primitive (media utility). No cover, no tutorial (static image — the default render IS the face). STRESS CATCH: HRI caption was mis-anchored since day one (xExpr 'w/2' = drawtext LEFT edge at center; hAlign lost) — fixed to true centering; default look shifts (caption centers), preview re-mint per the look-change rule, flagged for founder eyeball. Error-card visibility observation narrows the 2026-08-22 error-black candidate. Known physics: long payloads refuse below ~640px width (2 documented battery refusals)."
    }
  }
